# The Kernel's allowed third-party modules (docs/vision-v3/09a-ENGINEERING.md §2: "Go 1.25+, pure-Go
# SQLite, stdlib Ed25519"). One module path per line, no versions: go.sum pins those. The standard
# library is always allowed and never listed, which is why Ed25519 (crypto/ed25519) has no line.
#
# avk-boundary fails on any package in the Kernel's build, tests included, whose module is not named
# here, and on any `replace` directive, because a replace swaps the code behind an allowed name.
#
# Adding a line is a protected-base change (09a §14). A listed module does not admit its own
# dependencies; each needs its own line. B1-01a pinned modernc.org/sqlite v1.60.1 and lists its whole
# `go list -m all` closure below, measured offline against that pin: 23 modules besides sqlite. 9 of
# them compile into the Kernel's build (`go list -deps -test ./...`); the other 14 are SQLite's
# code-generation and test tooling, present in the module graph only.

